{
  "$comment": [
    "The author's labels for the two families the session record cannot settle. Written by reading each state, one at a time, before any door was asked. Committed so that the judgment is auditable rather than implicit in a build.",
    "progress: 'How close is the conversation to a resolved end?' 0 where the turn opens a topic or a new piece of work, 1 where it continues work already underway, 2 where it accepts, ships or winds up what was underway. Nothing later in the session settles this: a session that stops is a person walking away as often as it is work finished, so reading position off the record would be a proxy wearing an outcome's name.",
    "useful: 'Do the outputs help answer the user's request?' yes where the round returns something about the task — file contents, a test result, a compiler diagnostic, a push that landed, a status. no where the only content is the invocation failing: a blocked command, shell quoting that mangled the line, a binary that is not on the path. A compiler error is useful and a quoting error is not, which is the distinction the exit status cannot make and is the reason this is a reading rather than a rule over exit codes.",
    "Both are marked label_source `author` in the suite. Every other family there is `outcome`."
  ],
